      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before Europeans, the Mobilian tribe used Grand Bay’s coastal wetlands for fishing and trade along waterways to Mobile Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grand_bay_alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1870 completion of the New Orleans, Mobile and Texas Railroad spurred Grand Bay’s platting in 1871 on large lots for growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grand_bay_alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Grand Bay Land Company sold ten‑acre lots in the early 1900s, sparking settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Bay%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Grand Bay’s historic district, centered on the old bank building, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
